> Neglects to mention that Rogues are backstabing cowards.

That's because Rogues' backstabs are a "class modifier to a game
activity", in this case combat. If I were to attempt to stuff all
those into abil-343.txt, the main point of the file (level-gained
intrinsics) would be lost in the thicket.

As a combat modifier, backstabs are documented in weap-343.txt:

+   If you are a Rogue in natural form hitting a fleeing monster, aren't
    stuck or using two weapons, and subtotal B [[damage before
    artifact or jousting bonuses]] is more than one point, you strike
    from behind with an additional random damage from 1 to your
    experience level.

